{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Post-`8257` re-measurement of the 0031 and 0085 ranges — the first implementation step, done ahead of the claim.\n\nThe plan directs that the 0031 and 0085 citations be re-measured after `8257-3a28-e757-4079` runs, because those are the table's only two rows inside S3's 20-ADR set and S3's archive banner shifts every line below it. Measured against the `impl-8257` working tree (base `757ca4852d7`, with S3's edits applied and not yet landed).\n\nBoth files shift by exactly **+2 lines** — S3 adds 4 lines and removes 2 in each (`git diff --stat`: `4 +++-` on both).\n\n**ADR 0031** — `### Operator break-glass`\n\n| | Pre-S3 (plan as written) | Post-S3 (measured) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Heading | `:158` | `:160` |\n| Section | `:158-165` | `:160-167` |\n| Blank | `:166` | `:168` |\n| Next heading `## Lease self-healing (C2 — extends this module)` | `:167` | `:169` |\n\nLast content line is `:167`, \"lease interval automatically.\" The section's end is still 1 line clear of the next heading, so the hazard the earlier sweep caught — a range running 3 lines past the end and decapitating `## Lease self-healing` — does not reappear at the corrected range.\n\n**ADR 0085** — the two procedural sections\n\n| | Pre-S3 (plan as written) | Post-S3 (measured) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes` | `:58-71` | `:60-73` |\n| `### 4. Report` | `:73-79` | `:75-81` |\n| Next heading `## Consequences` | `:81` | `:83` |\n\n§3's last content line is `:73` (\"already-gone key re-raises the same eventual-consistency false-failure\"), `:74` is blank, and §4's last content line is `:81` (\"durable evidence … is recorded on ticket d01e\"), `:82` blank.\n\nTwo caveats, stated rather than assumed:\n\n1. These are measured against `8257`'s **unlanded** working tree. `8257` has passed its ACs and gates but has not yet been through `make verify`, Gerrit, or submit. If it changes before landing, re-measure; the +2 offset is a measurement, not a rule.\n2. The plan's instruction to anchor on **content** rather than line number still governs. These numbers are a convenience for the diff review, not a substitute for locating the headings at implementation time.\n\nThe other 7 ADRs in the table (0012, 0048, 0059, 0079, 0105, 0109, 0113) are outside S3's set and are unaffected; the previous sweep verified all 16 of their ranges exact at `757ca4852d7`.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793501428329051064,"uuid":"7449722a-b141-4c76-9030-6e892828ecde"}